// Reusable library node (execution_plan §11.1): drive the base (Nav2) to a site feature's approach point, then
// close onto its work pose (dock_at_feature standoff 0). Both are capabilities of the common boundary
// (openral_ext/capability_server/contracts.yaml), positional arguments in the contract's input order; no mission
// logic in the adapter (ros/plexil_capability_adapter).
//
// Result comes back through `ok` (InOut), not node outcome: a LibraryCall node's own outcome does not mirror its
// callee's by default (verified against 6.1.3 -- see docs/baselines/plexil.md), so every caller gates its next
// step on `ok` (PreCondition), the idiom PLEXIL's own regression tests use for a typed result
// (compilers/plexil/test/input/library-call1.ple).
//
// Nominal path only -- no retry/back-off yet. Failure kinds and reported stages for navigate_to_feature /
// dock_at_feature are still moving in a parallel session; see docs/baselines/plexil.md for the recovery set, TBD.

Boolean Command navigate_to_feature(String, Real);
Boolean Command dock_at_feature(String, Real, Real);

DriveAndDock:
{
  In String feature;
  In Real standoff_m;    // navigate_to_feature's stand-off along the feature's normal
  In Real approach_m;    // dock_at_feature's entry corridor length
  InOut Boolean ok;       // true on entry (the caller already gated on it); false on exit if either leg failed

  Nav:  { PreCondition ok; EndCondition isKnown(ok); PostCondition ok; ok = navigate_to_feature(feature, standoff_m); }
  Dock: { PreCondition ok; EndCondition isKnown(ok); PostCondition ok; ok = dock_at_feature(feature, 0.0, approach_m); }
}
